patrone-branding (0.1.3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Inter as the typeface everywhere, in place of Ubuntu Sans: the
    desktop, apps, window titles and the login screen (GNOME's font
    settings), and through fontconfig (05-patrone-fonts.conf) for
    sans-serif and for web pages and documents that ask for Segoe UI, in
    Chromium and other snaps too. Inter is close to Segoe UI, and is the
    font Patrone's own apps use. Depends on fonts-inter.
  * Name Settings' "Ubuntu Desktop" page "Desktop".

